</style>

<!-- HERO -->
<header class="post-hero">
  <div class="tags">
    <span class="tag tag-purple">Agentic Coding</span>
    <span class="tag tag-cyan">Test-Time Scaling</span>
    <span class="tag tag-green">Interactive</span>
  </div>
  <h1>Scaling Coding Agents with Rollout Summaries: RTV + PDR</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Standard test-time scaling — generate many attempts, pick the best — breaks for coding agents whose outputs are 40-step noisy trajectories rather than short answers.
    Meta's solution: compress each rollout into a structured summary first, then use recursive tournament voting to select the best, and feed those summaries to the next generation of rollouts.
    The result: Claude 4.5 Opus jumps from 70.9% → 77.6% on SWE-Bench Verified and 46.9% → 59.1% on Terminal-Bench v2.0.
  </p>
  <div class="post-hero-meta">
