<p>
  Notably, RTV alone (without PDR) already closes much of the gap — Claude Sonnet gains 6.2pp on SWE-Bench just from better parallel selection. PDR then adds another 2pp on top. The two methods are synergistic but independently valuable: RTV is a drop-in improvement for any system that already runs multiple agent rollouts; PDR requires an extra iteration but unlocks tasks that were unsolvable in the initial population.
</p>
