<!-- Listen-friendly content (hidden summary played during audio playback) -->
<div class="listen-friendly-content" style="display: none;" aria-hidden="true">
  <div lang="en">
    <h2>Audio Summary: Scaling Coding Agents with Rollout Summaries — RTV and PDR</h2>
    <p>Meta's new paper argues that test-time scaling for agentic coding is fundamentally a representation problem. Standard methods — generate many outputs, compare, pick the best — fail because each coding agent attempt is a 40-step noisy trajectory, not a short comparable answer. The solution is to first compress each trajectory into a compact structured summary capturing hypothesis, progress, failure mode, and remaining steps.</p>
    <p>These summaries enable two complementary scaling strategies. Recursive Tournament Voting, or RTV, runs pairwise comparisons between summaries in a tournament bracket, progressively eliminating weaker candidates with 8-vote majority decisions. Parallel-Distill-Refine, or PDR, feeds the top 4 summaries from iteration zero into a fresh generation of 16 rollouts — agents that already know what was tried, what failed, and what to try next. The combined PDR plus RTV pipeline improves Claude 4.5 Opus from 70.9% to 77.6% on SWE-Bench Verified and from 46.9% to 59.1% on Terminal-Bench v2.0. A striking side effect: after seeing prior summaries, agents solve problems in roughly half the steps.</p>
  </div>
  <div lang="zh">
    <h2>语音摘要：用轨迹摘要扩展编程智能体——RTV与PDR</h2>
    <p>Meta的这篇论文指出，智能体编程中的测试时计算扩展本质上是一个表征问题。传统方法——生成多个输出、比较、选最优——在智能体编程中失效，因为每次尝试都是长达40步的嘈杂轨迹，而非可直接比较的简短答案。解决方案是先将每条轨迹压缩为结构化摘要，包括假设、进展、失败原因和待完成事项。</p>
    <p>这些摘要支撑两种互补的扩展策略：递归锦标赛投票（RTV）对摘要进行两两比较，通过多轮淘汰逐步筛选最优候选；并行蒸馏精炼（PDR）将上一轮排名前K的摘要作为条件输入，指导新一轮16个智能体从已知假设出发重新求解。组合后的PDR+RTV流程将Claude 4.5 Opus在SWE-Bench Verified上从70.9%提升至77.6%，在Terminal-Bench v2.0上从46.9%提升至59.1%。一个令人惊喜的副作用是：经过摘要引导后，智能体解题所需步骤数减少了约一半。</p>
  </div>
</div>

